🐛 Describe the bug
C++ libotch1.7.1 cuda11.0
I put the data on cuda in a loop and then did a rot90 operation on the data, but the time was very erratic, up to 15ms, which was very strange
img_in = img_in.to(at::kCUDA);
while(1){
//code......
img_in = torch::rot90(img_in, 1, { (1), (2) });  //img_in.shap:[3,500,500]
//code.....
//Calculation time
}
The running time is between 0.01ms and 15ms, which is very abnormal and the time difference is very large.
